#: core/dynamic_preferences_registry.py:466
msgid ""
"This option determines whether the same customer (name and email address) "
"may register more than once for the same class series under the same name. "
"It is recommended to keep this disabled if you would like to keep precise "
"track of customer registration histories.  Drop-in registrations are not "
"counted when enforcing this rule, but if it is not enabled, then customers "
"will not be able to drop into a class series for which they have also "
"registered in full."
msgstr ""

#: core/dynamic_preferences_registry.py:486
msgid "Allow customers to register for a public event more than once"
msgstr ""

#: core/dynamic_preferences_registry.py:488
msgid ""
"This option determines whether the same customer (name and email address) "
"may register more than once for the same public event under the same name. "
"It is recommended to keep this disabled if you are collecting customer "
"information with your public event registrations and would like to keep "
"precise track of customer registration histories."
msgstr ""

#: core/dynamic_preferences_registry.py:507
msgid ""
"Allow customers to register as a drop-in for a class series more than once"
msgstr ""

#: core/dynamic_preferences_registry.py:510
msgid ""
"This option determines whether the same customer (name and email address) "
"may register more than once as a drop-in for the same class series under the "
"same name.  Drop-in registrations are typically not counted in customer "
"registration histories, so this is enabled by default, but you may choose to "
"disable it to enforce restrictions on repeated drop-in registrations."
msgstr ""

